WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.824
One filter is good, two filters are powerful.

2
00:00:03.824 --> 00:00:09.116
In this lesson, you will learn to extend a CALCULATE measure with a second

3
00:00:09.116 --> 00:00:14.408
filter, so you get the shipment amount for one salesperson and only delivered orders.

4
00:00:14.408 --> 00:00:15.920
Let's sharpen our numbers!

5
00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:22.863
On this page we have the overall shipment amount, forty four point seven million,

6
00:00:22.863 --> 00:00:27.925
and the total for salesperson S P zero one, three point six six million.

7
00:00:27.925 --> 00:00:31.180
I add a clear title for the next card.

8
00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:53.294
I copy the formula of SP01 Total Amount, and create a new measure:

9
00:00:53.294 --> 00:00:56.060
SP01 Total Amount That are Delivered.

10
00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:10.155
After the first FILTER, I add a comma and a second FILTER:

11
00:01:10.155 --> 00:01:13.392
the Shipments table, where Order Status equals Delivered.

12
00:01:13.392 --> 00:01:15.820
IntelliSense helps with every function name.

13
00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:27.631
CALCULATE now applies both filters together.

14
00:01:27.631 --> 00:01:32.680
Only rows for S P zero one that are delivered are added up.

15
00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:45.867
I put the new measure in a card. The result:

16
00:01:45.867 --> 00:01:47.650
two point eight seven million.

17
00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:53.000
Lower than three point six six, because some orders were not delivered. That makes sense!

18
00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:20.786
To check, I look at the tables in Table view:

19
00:02:20.786 --> 00:02:24.620
Shipments, with salesperson and order status, and Product, with its category.

20
00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:03.458
Next, I start a measure with three filters, adding a product, Milk Bars, from the Product table.

21
00:03:03.458 --> 00:03:07.080
Each filter narrows the result a little more. Great work!

